.TH LOUHI-CTL 1 2026-11-20 Louhi "Louhi"
.SH NAME
louhi-ctl \- Louhi's API from a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B louhi-ctl login
.B \-\-issuer
.I URL
.B \-\-client-id
.I ID
.B \-\-endpoint
.IR URL ...
.RB [ \-\-client-secret-file
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-scope
.IR SCOPE ...]
.br
.B louhi-ctl logout
.br
.B louhi-ctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENT ...]
.RB [ \-\-endpoint
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-ca
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-credentials
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B louhi-ctl
calls Louhi's HTTP API with a Lugh access token.
.B login
signs in once by Lugh's device flow and writes the issuer, client id,
endpoints and scopes to
.I ~/.config/louhi/config.yaml
and the tokens to
.IR ~/.config/louhi/credentials.yaml ,
readable only by the user. The access token is refreshed when less than a
minute of it is left. Given
.BR \-\-client-secret-file ,
a file only its owner may read holding a Lugh service principal's secret,
.B login
signs in by the client credentials grant instead, keeps the file's path and
never the secret, and asks for a new token with it when one runs out.
.B logout
removes the tokens.
.PP
Each call goes to the endpoints in turn until one answers: past one that
cannot be connected to, and for a read past one that gives no answer. A write
that may have reached a node is never sent to another.
.SH COMMANDS
.BR list-projects ,
.BR put-project ,
.BR describe-project ,
.BR put-quota ,
.BR describe-quota ,
.BR register-task-definition ,
.BR list-task-definition-families ,
.BR list-task-definitions ,
.BR describe-task-definition ,
.BR run-task ,
.BR list-tasks ,
.BR describe-task ,
.BR stop-task ,
.B logs
.RB ( \-\-container ,
.BR \-\-tail ,
.BR \-\-after ),
.BR list-nodes .
A command that takes a JSON document reads it from a file, or from standard
input given
.BR \- .
Each prints the answer's JSON.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOUHI_CONFIG
The configuration file, in place of
.IR ~/.config/louhi/config.yaml .
.TP
.B LOUHI_ENDPOINT
The endpoints, separated by commas or spaces.
.TP
.B LOUHI_CREDENTIALS
The credentials file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for a 2xx answer, 1 for any other answer or failure, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR louhi-node (1)
